# Grid A — S5 Enumerate (sub-package entry points)
#
# Targets: generic + ShapeListOfSymbols + ReqEnumeration. Exercises
# the enumerator's ability to resolve a DIRECTORY into its children
# (structural traversal) rather than symbol-by-symbol keyword search.
#
# Ground truth (current repo): 25 child package directories live under
# internal/analysis/. This case intentionally checks tail packages too so a
# lower-bound answer that only lists the first/main packages cannot pass.
ID="s5b"
NAME="enumerate — internal/analysis sub-packages"
QUESTION="列出 internal/analysis/ 下所有子包的目录名，以及每个子包的单一入口函数（entry-point function）。"
# 2026-05-14 strictness update: partial lower-bound answers often include the
# early/common packages but drop tail packages such as subject/sourcemix. Keep
# representative package anchors from the head, middle, and tail. Function-name
# regexes below include pair anchors for tail packages so merely mentioning them
# in a caveat cannot satisfy the case.
EXPECT_CONTAINS="normalizer compiler criterion gate subject sourcemix stopcond"
EXPECT_MATCHES_REGEX="\b(Normalize|InferScenario|Compile|Eval|EvalAll|Run|RunWith|BindByRelevance|Plan|Compute)\b
\b(Normalize|InferScenario|Compile|Eval|EvalAll|Run|RunWith|BindByRelevance|Plan|Compute)\b
\b(Normalize|InferScenario|Compile|Eval|EvalAll|Run|RunWith|BindByRelevance|Plan|Compute)\b
(subject.*Score|Score.*subject)
(sourcemix.*FromTemplateMix|FromTemplateMix.*sourcemix)
(stopcond.*ShouldStop|ShouldStop.*stopcond)"
EXPECT_NOT_CONTAINS=".java .py"
